From cbf82b123e5ad16a0536c9e7dc00518fb459ed8b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:57:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Release prefill lane on async admission failure; age lane
 ranks

Fix the prefill-lane scheduler livelock at max_parallel_prefills > 1:
the engine spins on empty steps (GPU idle, no forward dispatched)
while waiting requests monopolize the prefill lanes. Two defects, both
scheduler-side:

1. Intra-step leak: a lane-selected async KV-load candidate whose
   allocate_slots returns None takes the non-interleaved FCFS branch
   of the waiting loop and broke without releasing its lane,
   stranding the unprocessed lane-holders while _replenish refilled
   released lanes from the same never-scheduled cohort. Failed
   lane-holders are now parked and their lanes released (mirroring the
   interleaved path), so lanes rotate to the running chunks within the
   step. FCFS stop semantics are unchanged for non-lane requests
   (ready-imports escape preserved).

2. Cross-step monopoly: PrefillInterleaveStep is rebuilt every
   schedule() call, so intra-step parking cannot change the cross-step
   invariant; the cohort re-won every lane at rank -1 in begin_step,
   chunks were skipped in the preempt-capable first running pass, and
   the post-waiting pass is preemption-forbidden, pinning free == 0.
   The controller now tracks per-request lane-candidate attempts and
   rotates a never-scheduled request out of the front after
   LANE_AGING_STEPS consecutive attempts (bounded, deterministic, no
   env knobs), so chunks reach the preempt-capable pass and
   preemption frees blocks within a bounded number of steps.

Regression tests: tests/v1/core/test_prefill_lane_livelock.py
(test_async_admission_failure_releases_lane_for_other_candidates,
test_never_admissible_cohort_cannot_starve_runnable_chunk_forever).
